# Truth: whether a host value counts as true, as JavaScript's `if (value)` reads it. Absent, false, zero and the empty
# text are false, and every other value (a list, an object, a non-empty text, a non-zero number) is true. One task on
# every backend, over the compare module each platform already keeps (native/<platform>/compare.tree, decision 132):
# node and the browser ask the host's `Boolean`, Rust, Swift and Kotlin their compare runtime. It replaces the
# `bind is-truthy` copies the CLI's folders kept, each with a node case only (item term-self-host-001-1379).

mark stable

load @term/base/native/{platform}/compare
  find is-truthy, name host-is-truthy

task is-truthy
  take value, like dynamic
  like boolean
  send back
    call host-is-truthy
      read value
